WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.036 --> 00:00:02.045
- This puppy came for the milk taste test!

00:00:02.045 --> 00:00:03.401
(kissing sounds)

00:00:03.401 --> 00:00:05.458
I've had many types of milk,
but I've never had dog's milk.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.346
- I would never drink a glass of milk.

00:00:10.346 --> 00:00:11.507
- Oh, I would.

00:00:11.507 --> 00:00:13.051
- I drink milk every day.

00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:13.759
- Do you like milk?

00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:17.010
- Um, it's sort of, milk
kind of freaks me out.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.020
I drink a lot of soy milk.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:18.751
- Do you get farty?

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.214
(girl laughs)

00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:21.116
- It'll be good to find out

00:00:21.116 --> 00:00:22.769
if I'm lactose intolerant (laughs).

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:26.028
- It smells like a barn.

00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:26.937
- This one's heavier.

00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:28.817
(coughs in disgust)

00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:30.666
- Creamy, damn!
- Yeah.

00:00:30.666 --> 00:00:32.533
- Oh my god, I hate it.

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.710
- Something really depressed
produced this milk.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.740
- I do think goats are also weirdly

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.353
the children and spawn of Satan.

00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:41.001
- It's got that bitterness
to it that goat cheese has.

00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:42.661
- Have you seen a goat eye up close?

00:00:42.661 --> 00:00:45.006
Their pupils are rectangular.

00:00:45.006 --> 00:00:47.003
- I can't do it again,
I can't drink anymore.

00:00:47.003 --> 00:00:49.377
- This is goat's milk, and it's very good.

00:00:49.377 --> 00:00:51.144
- I just never wanted to lick a goat.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:55.014
- It almost smells like cookie dough.

00:00:55.014 --> 00:00:56.047
- Oh, that smells kind of sweet.

00:00:56.047 --> 00:00:56.725
- Yeah, fruity.

00:00:56.725 --> 00:00:58.346
Did you milk the teats of a fruit bat?

00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:00.053
- It's so sweet.

00:01:00.053 --> 00:01:01.153
- Ooh!

00:01:01.153 --> 00:01:03.559
- It tastes like a melted soft serve

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:05.184
that's been diluted, twice.

00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:06.288
- What about this is milk?

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:07.019
- It's white.

00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:09.863
- Full of water, cane
sugar, vanilla extract,

00:01:09.863 --> 00:01:10.862
that gives it the vanilla taste.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:12.232
- Oh, they faked it.

00:01:12.232 --> 00:01:13.822
- Flax seed milk, I like it.

00:01:13.822 --> 00:01:14.509
- Delicious.

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:15.158
- Mm hmm.

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:15.840
- I'd drink more.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.000
- I don't like this smell.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.993
- Oh this smells like another animal milk.

00:01:20.993 --> 00:01:21.896
- Smells cheesy.

00:01:21.896 --> 00:01:22.561
- Yeah.

00:01:22.561 --> 00:01:23.278
(grunts in disgust)

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.829
- I got at a chunk, immediately.

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:26.805
- Ugh!
- Didn't like it.

00:01:27.697 --> 00:01:28.441
- Nope.

00:01:28.441 --> 00:01:30.344
- I mean, it doesn't bad,

00:01:30.344 --> 00:01:32.183
but you saying that you had a chunk,

00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:33.257
- Right.
- Means I'm done.

00:01:33.257 --> 00:01:35.045
- This tastes like liquid mac and cheese.

00:01:35.045 --> 00:01:37.832
- There's a certain
distant staleness to it.

00:01:37.832 --> 00:01:38.897
- I didn't know sheep could milk.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.175
I mean, it makes sense,
they have babies, but like--

00:01:41.175 --> 00:01:42.638
- I don't think I like milk!

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:46.076
I came into this test loving milk,

00:01:46.076 --> 00:01:48.687
you hated milk, and now
I hate milk (laughs).

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:51.494
Our final milk.

00:01:51.494 --> 00:01:53.950
- It looks almost like, like white paint.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.107
- I don't have any floaters.

00:01:55.107 --> 00:01:56.234
- This one smells heavy.

00:01:56.803 --> 00:01:57.571
- What is this?

00:01:58.462 --> 00:01:59.241
- Not for me.

00:01:59.241 --> 00:01:59.894
- No.

00:01:59.894 --> 00:02:01.040
- It tastes like a corn husk.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:01.957
- It tastes like grass.

00:02:01.957 --> 00:02:03.281
- It tastes like grass!
- Grassy!

00:02:03.281 --> 00:02:07.033
- There's a millisecond
for which it is okay.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.415
Then, there's some horrible

00:02:09.415 --> 00:02:11.658
wood-ish taste.
- Yeah.

00:02:11.658 --> 00:02:13.335
- It's weird, it has a texture to it.

00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:15.178
- There's no way this
will get you high, right?

00:02:15.178 --> 00:02:16.420
- It's a "no" for the hemp milk.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:18.638
- First, I'm amazed at our ability

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.747
to make milk out of anything.

00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:21.752
- When we were kids, we only had one milk.

00:02:21.752 --> 00:02:22.597
- Yeah.
- Came from the cow.

00:02:22.597 --> 00:02:23.978
- My question is, how competitive

00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:25.479
is the fake milk industry?

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:26.848
- I don't know, I guess,

00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:28.355
I'll stick to soy milk.

00:02:28.355 --> 00:02:30.451
(girl laughs)
- There seems to be

00:02:30.451 --> 00:02:32.657
a lot of different companies.

00:02:32.657 --> 00:02:33.884
Are they neck and neck?

00:02:33.884 --> 00:02:34.729
Who's on top?

00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:36.111
- This is the milk you drink--
- Yeah.

00:02:36.111 --> 00:02:37.274
- After a hard day's work.

00:02:37.274 --> 00:02:39.182
Come home, you stand over your fireplace,

00:02:39.182 --> 00:02:41.044
you swirl the milk in a tumbler,

00:02:41.044 --> 00:02:42.827
you regret your life decisions,

00:02:42.827 --> 00:02:44.913
why you married Barbara so young,

00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:47.635
- And you drink this milk.
- And you drink this milk.

